{
  "dom_id": "step-e2210",
  "name": "Example: Dividing a Fraction by a Whole Number Using a Division Model",
  "problem": "Use the model below to calculate $\\dfrac{5}{6} \\div 4.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14133144/assets/d1c1c3842b04174137bfe8a938c70493493b2c9a0e74bee619d965446c9326a6.png)",
  "worked_solution": "Since we need to divide by $\\color{blue}4$, we split the whole into $\\color{blue}4$ equal parts horizontally.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14133144/assets/24bffed596b77ba53d57e04ebb6baede437d40f825c03a794ae7689f11c3c250.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents $\\dfrac{5}{24}$ of the whole.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{5}{6} \\div 4 = \\dfrac{5}{24} \\, .\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
